# 高频词汇 List01

## abandon
- **音标**: /əˈbændən/
- **词性**: v. / n.
- **释义**: 放弃；抛弃；放纵
- **例句**: He abandoned his plan to travel abroad.
- **近义词**: desert, forsake, give up
- **派生词**: abandonment (n.), abandoned (adj.)

## absorb
- **音标**: /əbˈsɔːrb/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 吸收；吸引；使全神贯注
- **例句**: The company absorbed the smaller firm last year.
- **近义词**: assimilate, take in, engage
- **派生词**: absorption (n.), absorbing (adj.)

## abstract
- **音标**: /ˈæbstrækt/
- **词性**: adj. / n. / v.
- **释义**: 抽象的；摘要；提取
- **例句**: The concept of beauty is abstract.
- **近义词**: theoretical, conceptual, summary
- **派生词**: abstraction (n.), abstracted (adj.)

## accelerate
- **音标**: /əkˈseləreɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 加速；促进
- **例句**: The government decided to accelerate economic reforms.
- **近义词**: speed up, quicken, hasten
- **派生词**: acceleration (n.), accelerator (n.)

## accumulate
- **音标**: /əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 积累；积聚
- **例句**: She accumulated a large fortune over the years.
- **近义词**: gather, amass, collect
- **派生词**: accumulation (n.), accumulative (adj.)

## acknowledge
- **音标**: /əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 承认；确认；致谢
- **例句**: He acknowledged his mistake publicly.
- **近义词**: admit, recognize, concede
- **派生词**: acknowledgment (n.)

## adapt
- **音标**: /əˈdæpt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 适应；改编
- **例句**: You must adapt to the new environment quickly.
- **近义词**: adjust, modify, acclimate
- **派生词**: adaptation (n.), adaptable (adj.)

## adequate
- **音标**: /ˈædɪkwət/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 充足的；适当的
- **例句**: The supply of food is adequate for the trip.
- **近义词**: sufficient, enough, satisfactory
- **派生词**: adequacy (n.), inadequately (adv.)

## advocate
- **音标**: /ˈædvəkeɪt/
- **词性**: v. / n.
- **释义**: 提倡；拥护者
- **例句**: She advocates equal rights for women.
- **近义词**: support, promote, champion
- **派生词**: advocacy (n.)

## aggressive
- **音标**: /əˈɡresɪv/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 侵略性的；有进取心的
- **例句**: The company adopted an aggressive marketing strategy.
- **近义词**: assertive, bold, combative
- **派生词**: aggressively (adv.), aggression (n.)

## allocate
- **音标**: /ˈæləkeɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 分配；拨出
- **例句**: The funds were allocated to education and healthcare.
- **近义词**: assign, distribute, designate
- **派生词**: allocation (n.)

## alter
- **音标**: /ˈɔːltər/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 改变；修改
- **例句**: They altered the plan at the last minute.
- **近义词**: modify, change, adjust
- **派生词**: alteration (n.), alternate (adj.)

## ambiguous
- **音标**: /æmˈbɪɡjuəs/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 模棱两可的；含糊的
- **例句**: The statement was deliberately ambiguous.
- **近义词**: vague, unclear, equivocal
- **派生词**: ambiguity (n.), ambiguously (adv.)

## anticipate
- **音标**: /ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 预期；期望
- **例句**: We anticipate a significant increase in demand.
- **近义词**: expect, foresee, predict
- **派生词**: anticipation (n.), anticipatory (adj.)

## apparent
- **音标**: /əˈpærənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 明显的；表面上的
- **例句**: It was apparent that she was not happy.
- **近义词**: obvious, evident, clear
- **派生词**: apparently (adv.)

## appropriate
- **音标**: /əˈprəʊpriət/
- **词性**: adj. / v.
- **释义**: 适当的；拨款
- **例句**: Please wear appropriate clothing for the occasion.
- **近义词**: suitable, proper, fitting
- **派生词**: appropriately (adv.), inappropriate (adj.)

## arbitrary
- **音标**: /ˈɑːrbɪtreri/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 任意的；武断的
- **例句**: The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.
- **近义词**: random, subjective, capricious
- **派生词**: arbitrarily (adv.), arbitrariness (n.)

## assess
- **音标**: /əˈses/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 评估；评定
- **例句**: Teachers assess students' progress regularly.
- **近义词**: evaluate, appraise, estimate
- **派生词**: assessment (n.), assessor (n.)

## assume
- **音标**: /əˈsjuːm/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 假定；承担
- **例句**: We cannot assume that everyone agrees.
- **近义词**: presume, suppose, undertake
- **派生词**: assumption (n.), assumed (adj.)

## authority
- **音标**: /ɔːˈθɒrəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 权威；当局
- **例句**: The local authority approved the building plan.
- **近义词**: power, jurisdiction, command
- **派生词**: authoritative (adj.), authorize (v.)
